Z||000000||beachbomb||06-04-2000||04:38 PM||||Hi all! Just to pass onto all of you the following info, just in case it happens to you. My 1984 Indy fiero 4 cyclinder's coolant fan (2 speed fan) would not come on and off at high temps like it was suppose to, would only come on if i turned on a/c, well after replacing sensors after sensors i finally got it right. On my car there are 3 coolant sensors. The one pointing towards the drivers seat runs the fan, replace it with a COOLANT TEMP "SENSOR", not a COOLANT TEMP "SWITCH", even Pontiac didn't know for sure which one it takes, after replacing and cursing alot i finally put the SENSOR in it and it works like a champ!! Hope this helps someone someday.||||reg||10
